Kind: widen
Issue: #935
Holds open: delays thread_create() 2 ms after thread_create_in() has returned.  In the fixed tree the thread is already listed and started by then, under the task lock, and the delay is harmless; with 935-start-after-return the thread is listed and not yet started for those 2 ms, which is the window in which act_test [54]'s task_terminate() reaches it, stops it and starts it through thread_unstop() before thread_create() starts it again
Run: --entry 14 300 -smp 4

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/thread.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/thread.c
index f02c3ed6..340ba2e7 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/thread.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/thread.c
@@ -1503,6 +1503,12 @@ thread_create(task_t task, thread_act_t *new_act)
 		return(rc);
 	}
 
+	{
+		extern void delay(int);
+
+		delay(2000);	/* 935-widen-create-start: hold the window before the start */
+	}
+
 	/*****
 	act_lock_thread(thr_act);
 	thread_dowait( thr_act, FALSE);
